---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PricingCalculator from '../../components/PricingCalculator.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Analytics Pricing Calculator"
  description="Compare estimated monthly costs for Google Analytics, Plausible, Fathom, Hotjar, and PostHog at your traffic level."
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="prose-width mb-8">
      <h1 class="section-heading text-gradient-primary">Pricing calculator</h1>
      <p class="page-intro mt-4">
        Compare estimated monthly costs across analytics platforms at your traffic level. Enter your
        monthly pageviews, optional custom events, and how many sites you track — we map each input to
        published pricing tiers and sort tools from lowest to highest estimated cost.
      </p>
    </header>

    <PricingCalculator />

    <section class="mt-10 card" aria-labelledby="how-estimates-work">
      <h2 id="how-estimates-work" class="font-heading text-lg font-semibold text-gradient-secondary">
        How estimates work
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          This calculator is a <strong class="text-fg">directional comparison</strong>, not a quote.
          It uses pricing tiers and project limits we maintain in our{' '}
          <a href="/tools/">tools directory</a>. When a vendor publishes clear tier tables, we map
          your inputs to the cheapest plan that fits. When pricing is usage-based or sales-led, we
          show <strong class="text-fg">Contact sales</strong> instead of guessing.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-fg">Pageviews</strong> drive Plausible, Fathom, and Hotjar estimates.
            Hotjar is approximated from pageviews (assuming ~3 pages per session).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-fg">Custom events</strong> are added to pageviews for event-based
            tools (PostHog, Umami, DataFast, Matomo Cloud).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-fg">Sites / projects</strong> can change the required plan: GA4 stays
            free across properties; Plausible switches to Growth for 2–3 sites; DataFast switches to
            Growth for 2–30 sites; Fathom, Hotjar, and Matomo Cloud are estimated per site.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-fg">What we do not model yet:</strong> annual discounts, add-ons,
          team seats, data retention upgrades, exact PostHog usage above 1M events, or enterprise
          contracts (GA4 360). Those need a vendor quote.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
        <a href="/methodology/">Read our full methodology →</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
